%%{init: {'theme':'dark'}}%%
%% Data flow - Request
%% Corrected 2026-08-23:
%%  - OpenWeatherMap -> yr.no (api.met.no)
%%  - merged two weather calls into one: the code makes ONE call to
%%    locationforecast/2.0/compact, and both current and forecast are
%%    derived from the same timeseries response
%%  - added the required headers and _meta on tools/call
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant W as Web Service (8080)
    participant A as Agent Service (8001)
    participant M as MCP Server (8000)
    participant O as LLM (Gemini)
    participant Y as yr.no (api.met.no)

    U->>W: What is the weather in Oslo?
    W->>A: POST /query
    Note over A: Load conversation history

    A->>O: Chat completion with tools
    O-->>A: Tool call: get_weather_forecast(Oslo)

    A->>M: POST /message - tools/call<br/>MCP-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28<br/>Mcp-Method: tools/call<br/>Mcp-Name: get_weather_forecast<br/>params._meta: protocolVersion + clientCapabilities

    Note over M: Geocode via Nominatim
    M->>Y: GET locationforecast/2.0/compact<br/>lat, lon
    Y-->>M: timeseries - one response
    Note over M: Derive current weather AND<br/>5-day forecast from one timeseries

    M-->>A: MCP response<br/>content, structuredContent, resultType
    Note over A: Parse structuredContent

    A->>O: Tool result + ask for an answer
    O-->>A: Natural-language response
    Note over A: Persist to the conversation DB

    A-->>W: JSON response
    W-->>U: Render the answer
